 ["Hooks Blizzard's shared tab plumbing (TabSystemMixin:SetTab, TabSystemOwnerMixin:SetTab, PanelTemplates_SetTab). Filtered on those functions' own `isUserAction` argument where they provide one, so a panel setting its own tab as it opens stays silent and only a tab YOU changed fires. Two known gaps: PanelTemplates_SetTab is the legacy path and has no such flag, so a few older panels may still fire on open; and the two mixin hooks only reach panels created AFTER Pulse loads, because Mixin() copies function references onto a frame at creation. Most big tabbed panels are load-on-demand and so are covered, but anything built before this addon isn't. Expect this one to be patchy."] = "Hooks Blizzard's shared tab plumbing (TabSystemMixin:SetTab, TabSystemOwnerMixin:SetTab, PanelTemplates_SetTab). Filtered on those functions' own `isUserAction` argument where they provide one, so a panel setting its own tab as it opens stays silent and only a tab YOU changed fires. Two known gaps: PanelTemplates_SetTab is the legacy path and has no such flag, so a few older panels may still fire on open; and the two mixin hooks only reach panels created AFTER Pulse loads, because Mixin() copies function references onto a frame at creation. Most big tabbed panels are load-on-demand and so are covered, but anything built before this addon isn't. Expect this one to be patchy.",
 ["Hooks StackSplitFrame:UpdateStackText."] = "Hooks StackSplitFrame:UpdateStackText.",
 ["Hostile target under reticle"] = "Hostile target under reticle",
 ["How far a motor has to move before the addon bothers telling the client about it. Raise it to cut the number of calls; too high and slow fades turn into visible steps. Shared by every channel — this is a call-rate setting, not a motor property."] = "How far a motor has to move before the addon bothers telling the client about it. Raise it to cut the number of calls; too high and slow fades turn into visible steps. Shared by every channel — this is a call-rate setting, not a motor property.",
 ["How far the hum swells either side of its baseline. 0 is a flat hold."] = "How far the hum swells either side of its baseline. 0 is a flat hold.",
 ["How fast the wingbeat-style undulation cycles."] = "How fast the wingbeat-style undulation cycles.",
 ["How long this motor takes to fall back toward silence. Too high and consecutive taps blur into one buzz; too low and sustained textures sound chopped. 0.028 reproduces the engine's old behaviour at 60fps."] = "How long this motor takes to fall back toward silence. Too high and consecutive taps blur into one buzz; too low and sustained textures sound chopped. 0.028 reproduces the engine's old behaviour at 60fps.",
 ["How long this motor takes to reach a new, stronger level during continuous textures. Higher is softer and more gradual; lower is snappier. 0.075 reproduces the engine's old behaviour at 60fps."] = "How long this motor takes to reach a new, stronger level during continuous textures. Higher is softer and more gradual; lower is snappier. 0.075 reproduces the engine's old behaviour at 60fps.",
 ["How many seconds before the scripted moment this fires."] = "How many seconds before the scripted moment this fires.",
 ["How often the hum swells, in cycles per second. 0.30 is roughly one slow breath every three seconds."] = "How often the hum swells, in cycles per second. 0.30 is roughly one slow breath every three seconds.",
 ["How often the lub-dub repeats while the warning stays active. Higher is more urgent; lower is less annoying. Independent of the screen flash's own (fixed, ~57 BPM) rate — this is a separate timer, not synced to it."] = "How often the lub-dub repeats while the warning stays active. Higher is more urgent; lower is less annoying. Independent of the screen flash's own (fixed, ~57 BPM) rate — this is a separate timer, not synced to it.",
 ["How pronounced each stroke is against its own baseline. Higher values (0.80-1.0) allow the counterweight to physically spin down during the glide phase between strokes. 0 is a flat drag with no rhythm at all."] = "How pronounced each stroke is against its own baseline. Higher values (0.80-1.0) allow the counterweight to physically spin down during the glide phase between strokes. 0 is a flat drag with no rhythm at all.",
 ["How sharply the high motor ramps in with speed. 1 = linear, higher = holds back more until near max speed. Only audible while actually gliding."] = "How sharply the high motor ramps in with speed. 1 = linear, higher = holds back more until near max speed. Only audible while actually gliding.",
 ["How steady the low motor stays regardless of speed. Only audible while actually gliding."] = "How steady the low motor stays regardless of speed. Only audible while actually gliding.",
 ["How strong the hum gets by the moment a regular cast completes. Only audible if \"Casting texture\" is also enabled on its own tab."] = "How strong the hum gets by the moment a regular cast completes. Only audible if \"Casting texture\" is also enabled on its own tab.",
 ["How strong the stealth hum is overall. Meant to sit just at the edge of perception — if you notice it as a vibration rather than a presence, it is too high."] = "How strong the stealth hum is overall. Meant to sit just at the edge of perception — if you notice it as a vibration rather than a presence, it is too high.",
