 ["Multiplies %s's high-motor intensity. 1.0 is the authored default; the top of this slider is where it stops making any further difference."] = "Multiplies %s's high-motor intensity. 1.0 is the authored default; the top of this slider is where it stops making any further difference.",
 ["Multiplies %s's low-motor intensity. 1.0 is the authored default; the top of this slider is where it stops making any further difference."] = "Multiplies %s's low-motor intensity. 1.0 is the authored default; the top of this slider is where it stops making any further difference.",
 ["Multiplies every impact, on top of each profession's own weight. Set it to zero for a craft you feel but never get hit by."] = "Multiplies every impact, on top of each profession's own weight. Set it to zero for a craft you feel but never get hit by.",
 ["Multiplies every impact, on top of each profession's own weight. Set to zero for a craft you feel but never get hit by."] = "Multiplies every impact, on top of each profession's own weight. Set to zero for a craft you feel but never get hit by.",
 ["Multiplies every trigger's intensity. Part of the current profile, not global."] = "Multiplies every trigger's intensity. Part of the current profile, not global.",
 ["Multiplies gait strength while mounted, on top of the racial mount's own weight. A kodo is already heavier than a hawkstrider before this touches it."] = "Multiplies gait strength while mounted, on top of the racial mount's own weight. A kodo is already heavier than a hawkstrider before this touches it.",
 ["Multiplies the baseline while fully submerged rather than bobbing at the surface, via IsSubmerged(). Set to 1.0 to feel the same either way. UNVERIFIED: IsSubmerged is confirmed present in the client API list, but whether it really distinguishes the two cases here has not been checked live."] = "Multiplies the baseline while fully submerged rather than bobbing at the surface, via IsSubmerged(). Set to 1.0 to feel the same either way. UNVERIFIED: IsSubmerged is confirmed present in the client API list, but whether it really distinguishes the two cases here has not been checked live.",
 ["Multiplies the continuous layer under every craft, on top of each profession's own weight. This is the part you feel for the whole craft rather than the individual blows."] = "Multiplies the continuous layer under every craft, on top of each profession's own weight. This is the part you feel for the whole craft rather than the individual blows.",
