 ["Navigation"] = "Navigation",
 ["Never miss an important group alert, even while looking away:\n• |cffffffffDirect Whispers:|r Distinct personal communication blip on incoming whispers.\n• |cffffffffParty & Raid Invites:|r Dual-pulse notification when receiving group invitations.\n• |cffffffffQueue Pops & Ready Checks:|r High-priority attention-grabbing pulse when instances are ready."] = "Never miss an important group alert, even while looking away:\n• |cffffffffDirect Whispers:|r Distinct personal communication blip on incoming whispers.\n• |cffffffffParty & Raid Invites:|r Dual-pulse notification when receiving group invitations.\n• |cffffffffQueue Pops & Ready Checks:|r High-priority attention-grabbing pulse when instances are ready.",
 ["New profile"] = "New profile",
 ["New setups enable casting, crafting, low-health and breath effects. Other effects start off; your saved choices are kept."] = "New setups enable casting, crafting, low-health and breath effects. Other effects start off; your saved choices are kept.",
 ["Next >"] = "Next >",
 ["Nintendo Switch Pro"] = "Nintendo Switch Pro",
 ["No legacy event for this one — it arrives only through the interaction manager, so it is silent if this client does not send that. Untested."] = "No legacy event for this one — it arrives only through the interaction manager, so it is silent if this client does not send that. Untested.",
 ["No rule"] = "No rule",
 ["Noisy. In a raid this event fires very frequently. Kept for completeness and defaulted off."] = "Noisy. In a raid this event fires very frequently. Kept for completeness and defaulted off.",
 ["None (full sensory richness)"] = "None (full sensory richness)",
 ["None (stock defaults)"] = "None (stock defaults)",
 ["Not filtered by rarity yet — fires for anything, common items included."] = "Not filtered by rarity yet — fires for anything, common items included.",
 ["Note the event name: Forever uses LEARNED_SPELL_IN_SKILL_LINE, not the older LEARNED_SPELL_IN_TAB, which is absent from this client's documentation entirely. Can fire more than once for a single visit to a trainer if you buy several ranks."] = "Note the event name: Forever uses LEARNED_SPELL_IN_SKILL_LINE, not the older LEARNED_SPELL_IN_TAB, which is absent from this client's documentation entirely. Can fire more than once for a single visit to a trainer if you buy several ranks.",
 ["Nothing about these is percussive, so they get the bed alone. Inventing a hammer for enchanting would be inventing a sensation that is not there."] = "Nothing about these is percussive, so they get the bed alone. Inventing a hammer for enchanting would be inventing a sensation that is not there.",
 ["OFF BY DEFAULT, and that is deliberate. A rolling swell suggests ocean, and this cue fires in rivers, lakes and canals too, where it would read as wrong rather than as atmosphere — Classic has no wave physics for it to be tracking, so it would be inventing something the world is not doing. Flat presence is the honest default. Raise it if you want a swell anyway; it is a good sensation, just not a true one."] = "OFF BY DEFAULT, and that is deliberate. A rolling swell suggests ocean, and this cue fires in rivers, lakes and canals too, where it would read as wrong rather than as atmosphere — Classic has no wave physics for it to be tracking, so it would be inventing something the world is not doing. Flat presence is the honest default. Raise it if you want a swell anyway; it is a good sensation, just not a true one.",
 ["ON — option changes and cue firings will print here."] = "ON — option changes and cue firings will print here.",
 ["Occurrence only, deliberately near-subliminal so it doesn't compete with \"Levelled up\". No size scaling: the amount would need UnitXP diffing and isn't worth the bookkeeping for a cue this quiet."] = "Occurrence only, deliberately near-subliminal so it doesn't compete with \"Levelled up\". No size scaling: the amount would need UnitXP diffing and isn't worth the bookkeeping for a cue this quiet.",
 ["Ocean Waves & Swell"] = "Ocean Waves & Swell",
 ["Ocean waves & swell"] = "Ocean waves & swell",
 ["Ocean zones only (guessed from zone name)"] = "Ocean zones only (guessed from zone name)",
 ["Off by default and deliberately the faintest cue in the addon: this fires for EVERY NPC you talk to, which in a city is constantly. Try it before leaving it on. Untested."] = "Off by default and deliberately the faintest cue in the addon: this fires for EVERY NPC you talk to, which in a city is constantly. Try it before leaving it on. Untested.",
 ["Off by default and mounted-only by default, on purpose: a texture that plays whenever you move is the most fatiguing thing in this addon and the most likely to make you switch it off wholesale. Uses shaped transient layers with fast-attack kicks and exponential decay to produce crisp, distinct footfalls without motor hum in between. Distinct timbres (boots, hooves, paws, heavy claws/pads, metal) drive both Low (body mass) and High (impact crispness) motors in concert. Speed is read out of combat only and held through a fight; snares and boosts are not tracked there, which is a deliberate trade for never touching a secret value. Goes quiet while swimming, flying, gliding, riding a flight path, or airborne after a jump — each of those has its own cue and footfalls have nothing to add to them."] = "Off by default and mounted-only by default, on purpose: a texture that plays whenever you move is the most fatiguing thing in this addon and the most likely to make you switch it off wholesale. Uses shaped transient layers with fast-attack kicks and exponential decay to produce crisp, distinct footfalls without motor hum in between. Distinct timbres (boots, hooves, paws, heavy claws/pads, metal) drive both Low (body mass) and High (impact crispness) motors in concert. Speed is read out of combat only and held through a fight; snares and boosts are not tracked there, which is a deliberate trade for never touching a secret value. Goes quiet while swimming, flying, gliding, riding a flight path, or airborne after a jump — each of those has its own cue and footfalls have nothing to add to them.",
 ["Off by default — a continuous texture, not a notification."] = "Off by default — a continuous texture, not a notification.",
 ["Off by default, layers with \"Low health\" rather than replacing it — same relationship as breathWarning/breathTexture. Same mechanism and same fullscreen-panel caveat as lowHealthWarning above. The shape itself is a code-level switch (Modules/Health.lua's HEARTBEAT_STYLE: smooth glow, flash-synced lub-dub, or an independently-timed lub-dub), not exposed here — flash-synced won out by feel. The knock's own gap/duration/intensity used to be four sliders here; fixed as plain constants in Modules/Health.lua once this exact combination was confirmed to feel right (2026-09-15)."] = "Off by default, layers with \"Low health\" rather than replacing it — same relationship as breathWarning/breathTexture. Same mechanism and same fullscreen-panel caveat as lowHealthWarning above. The shape itself is a code-level switch (Modules/Health.lua's HEARTBEAT_STYLE: smooth glow, flash-synced lub-dub, or an independently-timed lub-dub), not exposed here — flash-synced won out by feel. The knock's own gap/duration/intensity used to be four sliders here; fixed as plain constants in Modules/Health.lua once this exact combination was confirmed to feel right (2026-09-15).",
 ["Off by default, layers with \"Low on breath\" rather than replacing it."] = "Off by default, layers with \"Low on breath\" rather than replacing it.",
 ["Off by default. Suppresses \"Casting texture\" for the length of a craft so the two do not layer into one lumpy sensation. The profession is read by id from the recipe (C_TradeSkillUI.GetProfessionInfoByRecipeID), so no name matching and no localisation problem — but that field is documented nilable, and anything that does not resolve falls back to a generic work rhythm rather than going quiet. Gathering is NOT covered: swinging a pick at an ore node is not a recipe and has no recipe id. Per-profession toggles and strengths are on the Crafting page. Entirely untested."] = "Off by default. Suppresses \"Casting texture\" for the length of a craft so the two do not layer into one lumpy sensation. The profession is read by id from the recipe (C_TradeSkillUI.GetProfessionInfoByRecipeID), so no name matching and no localisation problem — but that field is documented nilable, and anything that does not resolve falls back to a generic work rhythm rather than going quiet. Gathering is NOT covered: swinging a pick at an ore node is not a recipe and has no recipe id. Per-profession toggles and strengths are on the Crafting page. Entirely untested.",
 ["Off means swings come from Forever's own PLAYER_SWING event — a real per-swing signal, confirmed non-secret and proven live. On forces the old prediction built from weapon speed instead. You should not need this: if Blizzard ever removes the event, Pulse detects that and falls back on its own. It exists so a patch that changes the event's BEHAVIOUR rather than removing it still leaves you a working cue."] = "Off means swings come from Forever's own PLAYER_SWING event — a real per-swing signal, confirmed non-secret and proven live. On forces the old prediction built from weapon speed instead. You should not need this: if Blizzard ever removes the event, Pulse detects that and falls back on its own. It exists so a patch that changes the event's BEHAVIOUR rather than removing it still leaves you a working cue.",
 ["Offensive"] = "Offensive",
 ["Offensive Combat Haptics"] = "Offensive Combat Haptics",
 ["Okay"] = "Okay",
 ["One cue for all four edges (top, bottom, left, right), observed via SmartNavigation's directional edge callbacks while keeping button selection isolated via polling to prevent execution taint. Standard default is off."] = "One cue for all four edges (top, bottom, left, right), observed via SmartNavigation's directional edge callbacks while keeping button selection isolated via polling to prevent execution taint. Standard default is off.",
 ["One cue for both directions, same reasoning as the navigation edge cue — a motor can't tell you which way you went."] = "One cue for both directions, same reasoning as the navigation edge cue — a motor can't tell you which way you went.",
 ["One full-bodied hit on both motors."] = "One full-bodied hit on both motors.",
 ["One long, sombre pulse when a spirit healer's window opens."] = "One long, sombre pulse when a spirit healer's window opens.",
 ["One pattern for every kind of refusal. May also do nothing inside dungeons and raids."] = "One pattern for every kind of refusal. May also do nothing inside dungeons and raids.",
 ["One sharp, heavy impact — fast attack, fast decay."] = "One sharp, heavy impact — fast attack, fast decay.",
 ["One strong, sustained pulse."] = "One strong, sustained pulse.",
 ["One sustained pulse."] = "One sustained pulse.",
 ["Only audible if \"Riding a flight path\" is also enabled on its own tab."] = "Only audible if \"Riding a flight path\" is also enabled on its own tab.",
 ["Only while mounted"] = "Only while mounted",
 ["Open Pulse settings"] = "Open Pulse settings",
 ["Other"] = "Other",
 ["Other crafting"] = "Other crafting",
 ["Overall gasp-knock strength — fixed per beat, not scaled by danger (2026-09-16: a danger-scaled lub/dub risked landing under the controller motor's own minimum activation threshold at low danger, causing missing \"dub\" knocks live). Urgency comes from heartRateCalm/heartRateCritical instead. Only audible if \"Underwater breath texture\" is also enabled on its own tab."] = "Overall gasp-knock strength — fixed per beat, not scaled by danger (2026-09-16: a danger-scaled lub/dub risked landing under the controller motor's own minimum activation threshold at low danger, causing missing \"dub\" knocks live). Urgency comes from heartRateCalm/heartRateCritical instead. Only audible if \"Underwater breath texture\" is also enabled on its own tab.",
 ["Overall heave amplitude of the oceanic swell. Sets the physical displacement intensity of the slow motor."] = "Overall heave amplitude of the oceanic swell. Sets the physical displacement intensity of the slow motor.",
 ["Overall intensity"] = "Overall intensity",
 ["Overall strength of each footfall before speed and state scaling."] = "Overall strength of each footfall before speed and state scaling.",
 ["Overall strength. Meant to sit at the edge of perception — if you notice it as a vibration rather than as being submerged, it is too high. Inherits the old idleFloatAmplitude, which was live-tuned to 0.04."] = "Overall strength. Meant to sit at the edge of perception — if you notice it as a vibration rather than as being submerged, it is too high. Inherits the old idleFloatAmplitude, which was live-tuned to 0.04.",
 ["Overdrive kick"] = "Overdrive kick",
 ["Overdrive time (s)"] = "Overdrive time (s)",
 ["Overwrite every motor's calibration with the selected controller's starting values. Ask first, because this discards any trimming you have already done."] = "Overwrite every motor's calibration with the selected controller's starting values. Ask first, because this discards any trimming you have already done.",
 ["Own motor"] = "Own motor",
 ["PLAYER_ALIVE also fires when you release to a graveyard, so this can fire while you are still a ghost."] = "PLAYER_ALIVE also fires when you release to a graveyard, so this can fire while you are still a ghost.",
 ["PLAYER_SOFT_ENEMY_CHANGED, an occurrence-only event with no payload at all — there is nothing here to come back secret. Fires on the soft target changing, which is not the same as actually targeting something; that's still \"Target changed\" on the Target & Focus page. Expect this to fire often while sweeping the camera through a crowd."] = "PLAYER_SOFT_ENEMY_CHANGED, an occurrence-only event with no payload at all — there is nothing here to come back secret. Fires on the soft target changing, which is not the same as actually targeting something; that's still \"Target changed\" on the Target & Focus page. Expect this to fire often while sweeping the camera through a crowd.",
 ["PLAYER_SOFT_FRIEND_CHANGED, occurrence-only, no payload. Worth pairing with the hostile cue above only if you can tell two TICKs apart — if not, give one of them a different shape with its own \"Feels like\" dropdown."] = "PLAYER_SOFT_FRIEND_CHANGED, occurrence-only, no payload. Worth pairing with the hostile cue above only if you can tell two TICKs apart — if not, give one of them a different shape with its own \"Feels like\" dropdown.",
 ["PLAYER_SOFT_INTERACT_CHANGED. Unlike its two siblings this one DOES carry a payload (oldTarget/newTarget GUIDs) and is flagged SecretWhenUnitIdentityRestricted in Blizzard's own docs, so this cue deliberately reads none of it and fires on the occurrence alone. Probably the most useful of the three: it's the one that says \"there is something here\" while you're looking around."] = "PLAYER_SOFT_INTERACT_CHANGED. Unlike its two siblings this one DOES carry a payload (oldTarget/newTarget GUIDs) and is flagged SecretWhenUnitIdentityRestricted in Blizzard's own docs, so this cue deliberately reads none of it and fires on the occurrence alone. Probably the most useful of the three: it's the one that says \"there is something here\" while you're looking around.",
 ["PLAYER_SOFT_TARGET_INTERACTION. Fires when native gamepad/action interact executes on the current soft target."] = "PLAYER_SOFT_TARGET_INTERACTION. Fires when native gamepad/action interact executes on the current soft target.",
 ["PULSE QUICK SETUP"] = "PULSE QUICK SETUP",
 ["Paced ranged rhythm with melee-weaving support. Auto-shot timing, weapon swings, pet status, trap triggers, and boss mechanics."] = "Paced ranged rhythm with melee-weaving support. Auto-shot timing, weapon swings, pet status, trap triggers, and boss mechanics.",
 ["Pacified or school-locked"] = "Pacified or school-locked",
 ["Page switches"] = "Page switches",
 ["Paladin"] = "Paladin",
 ["Pans left and right footfalls across the Low and High motors so the stride walks across your hands. Turn off for centered dual-motor footfalls."] = "Pans left and right footfalls across the Low and High motors so the stride walks across your hands. Turn off for centered dual-motor footfalls.",
 ["Party invite"] = "Party invite",
 ["Party leader changed"] = "Party leader changed",
 ["Passively polled by observing IsEnabled() on the currently focused element. Fires if the element becomes disabled while focused."] = "Passively polled by observing IsEnabled() on the currently focused element. Fires if the element becomes disabled while focused.",
 ["Passively polled from GamepadRadial:IsShown() to eliminate EventRegistry callback taint during radial menu activation."] = "Passively polled from GamepadRadial:IsShown() to eliminate EventRegistry callback taint during radial menu activation.",
 ["Passively polled from GamepadRadial:IsShown(). Picking a segment that opens a panel also closes the radial."] = "Passively polled from GamepadRadial:IsShown(). Picking a segment that opens a panel also closes the radial.",
 ["Passively polled from SmartNavigation focus state. Fires when controller navigation gains focus on a UI element."] = "Passively polled from SmartNavigation focus state. Fires when controller navigation gains focus on a UI element.",
 ["Passively polled from SmartNavigation focus state. Fires when controller navigation releases focus back to world control."] = "Passively polled from SmartNavigation focus state. Fires when controller navigation releases focus back to world control.",
 ["Passively polled from SmartNavigation's currentButton every 0.05s to eliminate execution taint when gamepad mode is toggled. Fires on real focus changes rather than stick motion. Gated on gamepad UI being active."] = "Passively polled from SmartNavigation's currentButton every 0.05s to eliminate execution taint when gamepad mode is toggled. Fires on real focus changes rather than stick motion. Gated on gamepad UI being active.",
 ["Passively polled via GetUIPanel every 0.05s to eliminate UIParentPanelManager execution taint on protected frames."] = "Passively polled via GetUIPanel every 0.05s to eliminate UIParentPanelManager execution taint on protected frames.",
